# Scramble API Docs (required per endpoint)

Docs UI: `/docs/api` · OpenAPI: `/docs/api.json` · Contract markdown: `docs/api/` · Skill: **`lancehive-api-docs`** + **`lancehive-api-contract`**

Package: `dedoc/scramble` · Base: **`/api/v1`**

Route file: `routes/features/v1/{feature}.php` · Controller/Resource: `app/Features/{Feature}/Http/` (no `V1/` subfolder).

## Every new/changed endpoint must

1. Register in `routes/features/v1/{feature}.php`, required from `routes/api.php` via `config('api.features_routes')` (Scramble `api_path` = `config('api.prefix')`).
2. Use a **Form Request** for body/query validation (Scramble infers request schema).
3. Return an **API Resource** (or `JsonResource` collection) — not raw arrays/models in controllers.
4. Add `#[Group('…', weight: N)]` on the controller class.

## Group weights (keep order stable)

| Group | weight |
|-------|--------|
| Authentication | 0 |
| Users | 1 |
| Settings | 15 |
| Admin | 10 |
| Tenancy | 20 |
| Clients / Projects / Tasks / Time Logs | 30–40 |
| Reports | 45 |
| Client Invoices | 50 |
| Subscriptions | 60 |

Use `#[Endpoint(title: '…', description: '…')]` when the method name is not self-explanatory.

## Tenant routes

Class-level header on tenant controllers:

```php
use Dedoc\Scramble\Attributes\HeaderParameter;

#[HeaderParameter('X-Freelancer-Id', description: 'Active freelancer workspace ID', required: true)]
#[Group('Clients', weight: 30)]
```

List endpoints: document `per_page` (max 100) and `cursor` via Form Request or `#[QueryParameter]`.

## Auth

`auth:sanctum` routes are auto-marked bearer-auth (`config/scramble.php` security_strategy). Public routes stay unauthenticated.

## Verify before done

```bash
vendor/bin/sail artisan test --compact tests/Feature/Api/DocumentationTest.php
```

Add the new path to `DocumentationTest` (or a feature-scoped doc test) — assert `paths` contains the route.

## Contract markdown (keep in sync)

When adding/changing endpoints, update matching `docs/api/endpoints/{group}.md` — auth, middleware, request, response, **Errors** table. Cross-check `docs/api/errors.md`.

## Do not

- `#[ExcludeRouteFromDocs]` unless truly internal.
- Return untyped `response()->json([...])` for new endpoints — blocks accurate response schemas.
- Skip doc test updates when adding routes.
- Skip `docs/api/` update when request/response shapes change.
